# Development

Initialize the module with `go mod init {{project_slug}}`, or use the intended
remote module path and replace `{{project_slug}}/internal/` in the Go imports.
Resolve the dependencies before running the Makefile:

```sh
go get github.com/spf13/cobra github.com/spf13/viper golang.org/x/term go.yaml.in/yaml/v3 github.com/stretchr/testify
go mod tidy
make install
```

Install golangci-lint using its official installation instructions. `make install`
downloads modules and installs goimports and gotestsum when they are missing.
Run `make help` for all targets. The binary entry is the project root.

```sh
make fmt-check tidy-check build vet lint test test-integration smoke coverage
```

`make fmt` applies gofmt and goimports. Unit tests use testify and live beside
the code. Integration tests have the `integration` build tag; their `TestMain`
builds one binary for the suite and each case runs it in an isolated directory.
`make vet` and golangci-lint include this tag. `make coverage` runs unit tests
with the race detector and enforces the Makefile's coverage floor; it needs cgo.

`make build` embeds version, commit and build time through linker flags.
Without linker flags, `go run . --version` prints the development default.
`make vuln` checks reachable dependency vulnerabilities. `make ci` runs the
checks used in CI. Fill the README's `stacks:fill` markers before the project's
`stacks verify` can pass its README check.
